course: dictionary
lesson: 4509
title: One word, two meanings: hazelnut
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can name a thing, and it can also describe something. Hazelnut is a noun, and its main meaning is the small, round, brown nut of the hazel tree, with a hard shell. The sentences tell you which meaning is used. «A dormouse leaves a smooth round hole with tooth marks around the edge in a hazelnut» is about the nut itself.
explain: Look for clue words. «The hazel dormouse gets very fat in autumn on hazelnuts and berries» tells you that hazelnuts are food, eaten by an animal before winter. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check: a small, round, brown nut still makes sense there, so you have the right meaning.
explain: When hazelnut comes before another word, as in «chocolate hazelnut spread», it often tells you the flavour of the thing. In «hazelnut tree», it tells you which tree grows the nuts. Read the words after it to see which job it is doing.
fact: A hazelnut is the small, round, brown nut of the hazel tree, with a hard shell.
fact: Hazelnut can also describe a flavour, as in «chocolate hazelnut spread».
fact: Squirrels and dormice eat hazelnuts; a dormouse leaves a smooth round hole with tooth marks around the edge.
fact: Some people get very ill from nuts, so schools often ban them.
fact: «Hazel dormice in Britain have fallen by about half since 2000, reported.»
exercise: What is a hazelnut? | A bird that lives in woods | A type of hard stone | *A small, round, brown nut from the hazel tree
exercise: «A dormouse leaves a smooth round hole with tooth marks in a hazelnut.» Which animal left the marks? | A volunteer | *A dormouse | Rain | A squirrel
exercise: «The hazel dormouse gets very fat in autumn on hazelnuts and berries.» Find and copy one word that tells you when. | winter | berries | fat | *autumn
test: «Look at a squirrel's teeth when it cracks a hazelnut: they are orange.» What is the squirrel cracking? | *A nut with a hard shell | A stone | A berry | A leaf
test: In «chocolate hazelnut spread», what does hazelnut describe? | A shell | *The flavour of the spread | A tree | A squirrel
exam: Why do schools often ban hazelnuts? | *Because some people get very ill from nuts | Because they are always rotten | Because squirrels steal them | Because they are too big for lunchboxes
